**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{10\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=10\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"} :step/id #uuid "e15523fe-4f49-557d-ba8f-2d82dda09940" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522893}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522893 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "341cebc5-0086-51c4-a7a7-568caded3433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522137} {:answer/id #uuid "38beef69-795f-5e94-844c-2d988f85a1fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522142} {:answer/id #uuid "4e9b4350-82ac-5374-a266-911f01cdc03d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522187} {:answer/id #uuid "c6087914-80dd-50e5-8ee5-7f3d56af6f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522432} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9fc8b3-618d-5488-9e40-7e984f38b54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522483}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522483} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d37eb1-f3c7-5886-b6e4-e84343d1696f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9ac4e11-4390-5ef8-897e-a450b29b74cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-149679" :question/problem "The 